---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ISSUES_URL } from '../lib/site';
import { linkAttrs } from '../lib/external-link';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site does and does not collect: no accounts, no cookies, no tracking of individual visitors, and your location never leaves your browser.">
	<div class="prose">
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="muted">Last updated 17 October 2026</p>

		<p>
			Recreational Drones is a free guide to drone rules, run as a personal project. It is built to need as little
			about you as possible.
		</p>

		<h2>What we collect</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Nothing that identifies you.</strong> There are no accounts, no forms, no cookies and no advertising. A
			test checks that a visit sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser.
		</p>
		<p>
			We do use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to count visits and page views, so we can see which
			guides people read. Cloudflare says it does not track individual visitors, and it does not use cookies or save
			anything in your browser. It gives us totals, such as which pages were viewed, which countries visits came
			from, and which kinds of device and browser were used. See
			<a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" {...linkAttrs("https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/")}>how Cloudflare Web Analytics works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Your location</h2>
		<p>
			The map has a button that finds where you are. It asks your browser for your position only when you press it,
			and your browser asks your permission first. The position is used in your browser to work out which country you
			are in. It is not sent to us or to anyone else, and it is not stored. You can refuse, and search for a country
			instead.
		</p>

		<h2>Who hosts the site</h2>
		<p>
			The site runs on Cloudflare. As with any website, the host receives your IP address and the details of each
			request (the page asked for, your browser and device type) in order to send you the page, and it may keep
			standard server logs. We do not use that information, and we do not get it. See
			<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" {...linkAttrs("https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/")}>Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Links to other sites</h2>
		<p>
			Each guide links to the official authority it is based on, and some to other sites. Those sites have their own
			privacy practices, which we do not control.
		</p>

		<h2>Reporting a mistake</h2>
		<p>
			If you report a mistake, you do it on GitHub, which has its own privacy policy. A GitHub issue is public, and
			shows your GitHub username. See <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>
			If this ever changes, we will update this page first and say what is collected and why. The history of this page is in <a href={ISSUES_URL.replace('/issues', '')} {...linkAttrs(ISSUES_URL)}>the project on GitHub</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
